<BaseLayout title="Returns & Repairs | David Dindi" description="A clear framework for product concerns, returns and repair enquiries.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/policies/how-to-order/">Policies</a> / Returns & Repairs</div><span class="eyebrow">Customer information</span><h1>Returns & Repairs</h1><p class="lead">A clear framework for product concerns, returns and repair enquiries.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container content">
    <h2>Contact us promptly</h2>
    <p>If an item arrives damaged, appears faulty or differs from the confirmed order, contact the business with the order details and clear photographs so the concern can be assessed.</p>
    <h2>Natural leather characteristics</h2>
    <p>Natural variations in grain, colour and visible marks may be part of the material and are explained in our <a href="/leather-philosophy/">leather philosophy</a>. This does not exclude customer rights relating to genuine defects or non-conforming goods.</p>
    <h2>Repairs</h2>
    <p>Repair requests should be assessed individually. Any repair options, costs, transport arrangements and expected timeframes must be agreed before work begins.</p>
    <div class="notice"><strong>Owner and legal review required:</strong> this is not a complete final returns policy. Confirm return timeframes, condition requirements, return shipping, custom-order rules, refunds, repair terms and warranty commitments. Check South African consumer-law requirements before publication.</div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>